      ":question/id": "e9c4753d-4b2b-5a63-8156-0a2eb7bb718e",
      ":question/problem": "An aquarium initially holds $100L$ of water containing $3kg$ of dissolved minerals.\nA solution containing $0.04kg/L$ of dissolved minerals is pumped into the aquarium at a rate of $8L/min$, while the completely mixed water is drained out at a rate of $12L/min$. If the amount of minerals $Q(t)$, in kilograms, in the tank $t$ minutes after pumping begins is given by\n$Q(t) = \u03b1(1 - \\frac{t}{25}) + \u03b2(1 - \\frac{t}{25})^{3}$\nwhere $\u03b1$ and $\u03b2$ are constants, what is the value of $\u03b1 + \u03b2$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
